        "title": "COVID and the Four Categories of Value",
        "principle": "Writing amid a pandemic year of falling operating earnings and a $11 billion write-down, Buffett reframes Berkshire's worth around four flagship holdings, its insurance operation, BNSF, its Apple stake, and BHE, and argues that share buybacks, not big new deals, are the surest way to hand shareholders a larger claim on all of them.",
