        "title": "Chapter 9: Tortured into Greatness",
        "principle": "As Nvidia scaled past 5,700 employees, Jensen replaced hierarchy with public feedback, a flat 40-plus-direct-report structure, mission-driven 'Pilot in Command' ownership, mandatory Top 5 status emails, and whiteboard-only meetings to keep the company moving like a small one.",
