        "principle": "Demanding a 'justification' for relying on our best theories is a misconceived demand: it either regresses infinitely or ends in dogmatism, and Popperian fallibilism escapes it by never claiming justified certainty in the first place, only tentative, well-argued explanations that have survived criticism better than their actual rivals.",
